                        <h1>
                            Proofs of three conjectured internal congruences modulo 32 for Schur-type overpartitions
                        </h1>
                        <div class="prodhead">

                            <div class="specs tablespecs">
                                                                                                <div class="specrow"><span class="speclabel"><strong>Published in:</strong> </span><span
                                        class="specvalue"><a
                                            href="/products/12/Journals/Quaestiones Mathematicae">
                                            Quaestiones Mathematicae </a><br>
                                        <a
                                            href="/products/12/Journals/Quaestiones Mathematicae#volume48">Volume
                                            48 </a>, <a
                                            href="/products/12/Journals/Quaestiones Mathematicae#issue48-4">issue
                                            4</a>,
                                        pages:
                                        611–621 </span></div>
                                

                                <div class="specrow"><span class="speclabel"><strong>DOI:</strong> </span><span
                                        class="specvalue">
                                        10.2989/16073606.2024.2411627 </span></div>
                                <div class="specrow"><span class="speclabel"><strong>Author(s):</strong> </span><span
                                        class="specvalue">
                                        <span class="authorname"><span class="author"><a href="https://nisc.com/search/author/Weifeng%20Gao" rel="nofollow">Weifeng Gao</a></span><span class="authoraffiliation">School of Mathematical Sciences, Suzhou University of Science and Technology, P.R. China</span>, </span><span class="authorname"><span class="author"><a href="https://nisc.com/search/author/Olivia%20X.M.%20Yao" rel="nofollow">Olivia X.M. Yao</a></span><span class="authoraffiliation">School of Mathematical Sciences, Suzhou University of Science and Technology, P.R. China</span>, </span>                                    </span></div>

                                <!-- Keywords -->
                                <div class="specrow">
                                    <span class="speclabel"><strong>Keywords:</strong> </span>
                                    <span class="specvalue">
                                        <a href="/search/kw/Primary%3A+Primary%3A+11P83" rel="nofollow">Primary: Primary: 11P83</a>, <a href="/search/kw/Secondary%3A+05A17" rel="nofollow">Secondary: 05A17</a>, <a href="/search/kw/Partitions" rel="nofollow">Partitions</a>, <a href="/search/kw/Schur-type+overpartitions" rel="nofollow">Schur-type overpartitions</a>, <a href="/search/kw/congruences" rel="nofollow">congruences</a>, <a href="/search/kw/theta+function+identities" rel="nofollow">theta function identities</a>, <a href="/search/kw/%28p" rel="nofollow">(p</a>, <a href="/search/kw/k%29-parameterization+of+theta+functions" rel="nofollow">k)-parameterization of theta functions</a>,                                     </span>
                                </div>


                            </div>
                            <div class="specs abstractions"><a href=" https://doi.org/10.2989/16073606.2024.2411627" target="_blank"
                                    class="fulltextlink">Download full text</a>
                                <a class="fulltextlink issuealerts" href="#">Get new issue alerts</a>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <hr class="abhr">
                        <div class="specs abouttext">
                            <h3>Abstract</h3>
                            Let <em>S</em>(<em>n</em>) denote the number of overpartitions of Schur-type. Recently, Chern, da Silva and Sellers proved many congruences modulo 8 and 16 for <em>S</em>(<em>n</em>). At the end of their paper, they also posed a conjecture on internal congruences modulo 32 for <em>S</em>(<em>n</em>). In this paper, we confirm their conjecture by using theta function identities and the (<em>p</em>, <em>k</em>)-parameterization of theta functions given by Alaca and Williams. In particular, we show that for any integer <em>j</em> with 0 ≤ <em>j</em> ≤ 31, there are infinitely many integers <em>u<sub>j</sub>
               </em> such that <em>S</em>(<em>u<sub>j</sub>
               </em>) ≡ <em>j</em> (mod 32).
                        </div>
